,"intro":"<p class=\"intro-lead\">If you want to get into the Star Wars novels and comics, you're in the right place.</p><div class=\"intro-tags\"><span class=\"itag\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg>I'm assuming that if you're here, you've already watched the animated and live-action media.</span></div><details class=\"cuts\"><summary>What's left out, and why<span class=\"n\">2 entries</span><svg class=\"chev\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"cuts-body\"><p class=\"cuts-prose\" style=\"margin:0 0 .6rem\">The omitted media are the same as on the main timeline, except <strong>The Acolyte</strong>, which may be worth watching if you read the comics: it's the only screen production (besides <strong>Star Wars: Young Jedi Adventures</strong>) set during the High Republic.</p><p class=\"cuts-prose\" style=\"margin:0 0 .6rem\">The omitted comics are throwaway one-shots, comics aimed at young children, or adaptations of screen productions.</p></div></details>"
